1
00:08:54,000 --> 00:09:00,000
For the first time... the vast, spectacular drama that changed the world!

2
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:54,000
The Message is a adventure, drama, action film directed by Moustapha Akkad.

3
00:26:42,000 --> 00:26:48,000
In sixth-century Mecca, Prophet Muhammad receives his
first revelation from God as a messenger.

4
00:35:36,000 --> 00:35:42,000
Three years later, he's not alone in his quest and
publicly declares his prophecy.

5
00:44:30,000 --> 00:44:36,000
Muhammad is fought by Abu Sufian and his wife Hind, rulers of Mecca.

6
00:53:24,000 --> 00:53:30,000
Muhammad's followers are hunted and tortured but he continues his calling.

7
01:02:18,000 --> 01:02:24,000
Hamza, played by Anthony Quinn.

8
01:11:12,000 --> 01:11:18,000
Hind, played by Irene Papas.

9
01:20:06,000 --> 01:20:12,000
Abu Sufyan, played by Michael Ansara.

10
01:29:00,000 --> 01:29:06,000
Bilal, played by Johnny Sekka.

11
01:37:54,000 --> 01:38:00,000
Khalid, played by Michael Forest.

12
01:46:48,000 --> 01:46:54,000
Ammar, played by Garrick Hagon.

13
01:55:42,000 --> 01:55:48,000
The Message (Arabic: الرِّسَالَة, romanized: Ar-Risālah) originally known as Mohammed, Messenger of God (Arabic: مُحَمَّد رَسُول‌ الله, romanized: Muḥammad Rasūl
Allāh) is a 1976 epic film directed and produced by Moustapha Akkad that chronicles the life and times of Muhammad, who is never directly depicted.

14
02:04:36,000 --> 02:04:42,000
Released in separately filmed Arabic- and English-language versions, The
Message serves as an introduction to the early history of Islam.

15
02:13:30,000 --> 02:13:36,000
The international ensemble cast includes Anthony Quinn, Irene Papas, Michael Ansara, Johnny
Sekka, Michael Forest, André Morell, Garrick Hagon, Damien Thomas, and Martin Benson.

16
02:22:24,000 --> 02:22:30,000
It was an international co-production between Libya,
Morocco, Lebanon, Syria and the UK.

17
02:31:18,000 --> 02:31:24,000
The film was nominated for Best Original Score in the 50th Academy Awards, composed by
Maurice Jarre, but lost the award to Star Wars (composed by John Williams).

18
02:40:12,000 --> 02:40:18,000
The film explores themes of middle east, muslim, islam, religion, muhammad.

19
02:49:06,000 --> 02:49:12,000
The tone is emotional.
